ion (2) (the bound \\(t\\le 3\\)) was derived from a flawed argument (Critical Error 8).  \n- The constructions claimed to exhibit the required configurations are invalid (Critical Errors 9, 10, 11).  \n- Therefore the final conclusion is unsupported. **Incorrect.**\n\n---\n\n## Overall Assessment\n\nThe solution fails to provide a correct upper bound on the number of sunny lines and presents constructions that do not actually cover all required lattice points nor contain the prescribed number of lines. These constitute **Critical Errors** that break the logical chain of the proof. Consequently, the answer “\\(\\{0,1,2,3\\}\\)” is not justified, and the solution is **invalid**."
